WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.422 --> 00:00:04.510
Unit twenty-four. Giving Robots Instructions!

2
00:00:05.455 --> 00:00:10.179
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emily, your technology teacher.

3
00:00:10.229 --> 00:00:14.184
Hi, Ms. Emily! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:14.234 --> 00:00:18.672
Today we learn about Giving Robots Instructions. Let's go!

5
00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:23.251
Robot. Say it with me. Robot!

6
00:00:26.745 --> 00:00:30.678
Command. Say it with me. Command!

7
00:00:34.121 --> 00:00:37.940
Forward. Say it with me. Forward!

8
00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:44.957
Turn. Say it with me. Turn!

9
00:00:48.512 --> 00:00:52.633
Left. Say it with me. Left!

10
00:00:56.152 --> 00:00:59.913
Right. Say it with me. Right!

11
00:01:03.419 --> 00:01:07.006
Stop. Say it with me. Stop!

12
00:01:10.425 --> 00:01:14.441
Program. Say it with me. Program!

13
00:01:18.019 --> 00:01:31.550
A robot needs a command for each move: forward, turn left, turn right... / stop. Putting commands together makes a program. If the robot goes the wrong way, I fix the program.

14
00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:34.974
Now I understand. Thank you, Ms. Emily!

15
00:01:35.699 --> 00:01:40.948
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:40.998 --> 00:01:42.148
Forward!

17
00:01:43.152 --> 00:01:48.684
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:48.734 --> 00:01:49.884
Stop!

19
00:01:50.684 --> 00:01:57.700
Did you know? Some classroom robots can be programmed just by pressing arrow buttons on their backs!

20
00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:00.060
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:02:00.993 --> 00:02:09.204
Think and answer. How would you tell a robot to walk to the door?

22
00:02:09.254 --> 00:02:10.404
Great answer!

23
00:02:11.461 --> 00:02:17.137
Great job today! Keep learning, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:17.187 --> 00:02:20.175
Goodbye, everyone! See you next time!

